{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>כחצות (about midnight).</b> In the strategy of a king of flesh and blood, when a province rebels against him: first he breaches their water channel — thus the Holy One, blessed be He, brought blood, and they could not drink from the water. Then he brings heralds to sound against them with trumpets and shofar — thus the frogs. Then he shoots arrows at them — thus the lice, which enter into them like an arrow. Then he brings barbarians, i.e. a mixed rabble, and thus [was] the ערוב (wild swarms). Then he brings men to plunder their livestock — thus the pestilence (דבר). Then he sends upon them naphtha and every foul odor to defile them — thus the boils (שחין), which stank. Then [he sends] sling-stones — thus the hail. Then he brings multitudes to consume their crops — thus the locusts. Then he imprisons [them] in the prison house — thus the darkness. Then he kills all the great and small among them — thus the plague of the firstborn. And everything the Holy One, blessed be He, brought upon the Egyptians, He is destined to bring upon the nations of the world (עכו\"ם): blood, as we say: ״ונתתי מופתים וגו'״. Frogs — their voice is harsh, and likewise upon the nations: ״קול שאון מעיר״. The dust of Egypt [turned] to lice — thus upon the nations: ״ונהפכו נחליה וגו'״. ערוב — as it is written: ״וירשוה קאת וקפוד וגו'״. דבר — as it is written: ״ונשפטתי אתו בדבר וגו'״. שחין — as it is written: ״וזאת המגפה וגו'״. Hail — as it is written: ״ואבני אלגביש״. Locusts — as it is written: ״אמור לצפור כל כנף ולכל חית השדה הקבצו וגו'״. Darkness — as it is written: ״ונטה עליה קו תהו ואבני בהו״. Plague of the firstborn — as it is written: ״והיו לשמה נסיכי צפון״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The heading כחצות matches Exodus 11:4. נפט is read as naphtha (bitumen/pitch); ברברים as barbarians, glossed by the compiler as עם כל (a mixed rabble). The verse fragments cited for the eschatological plagues on the nations are drawn from various prophetic books (e.g. Joel, Isaiah, Zephaniah) without addresses, as is standard in this compilation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:00.818708098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}